Hunt: Microsoft Teams now acting as C2:

Command and Control infrastructure enabling Red Teamers to execute system commands on compromised hosts via Microsoft Teams. 
It embeds data into hidden span tags within Microsoft Teams messages and exfiltrates command results through Adaptive Cards image URLs, triggering out-of-bound requests to a C2 server. 
The absence of direct communication between the victim and attacker, along with the victim only sending HTTP requests to Microsoft servers and antiviruses not scanning MS Teams log files, 
makes detection more challenging.

// Query to find execution of specific commands or executables

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine has "wget" and ProcessCommandLine has "https://github.com/cxnturi0n/convoC2/releases/download/v0.1.0-alpha/convoC2_server_amd64.tar.gz" and ProcessCommandLine has "tar -xzvf convoC2_server_amd64.tar.gz --one-top-level"
    or ProcessCommandLine has "convoC2"
    or ProcessCommandLine has "convoC2_agent.exe -h"
| project Timestamp, DeviceName, FileName, ProcessCommandLine, InitiatingProcessFileName, InitiatingProcessCommandLine, ReportId

